---
description: Context-first repository memory and token-efficient task routing
alwaysApply: true
---

Before searching source, read `CONTEXT-MAP.md`, route the task to the smallest owning context, and read that `docs/contexts/<context>/CONTEXT.md`.

For a scoped task, start from documented Primary Entry Points. Do not re-audit repository architecture merely for reassurance.

Use FAST/SURGICAL by default. Escalate to DEEP only when ownership is unclear, code contradicts memory, the task crosses domains, or it changes DB/RLS/auth/security/public contracts.

Prefer smallest valid change, targeted validation, and stop when acceptance criteria pass.
